From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:15:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: let the interrupt thread finish before
 masking for D3

brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3() masks and clears the device's interrupts once
the D3 ACK is in. When the ACK came as a control message, it is
published from brcmf_pcie_rx_process() in the interrupt thread, which
then goes on: it reads the state, re-enables the interrupt while it is
still STATE_UP and kicks the D2H poll. If that happens after the
suspend path masked the interrupt, the device is left unmasked across
D3, and a later interrupt in D3 runs the handler against a sleeping
device.

Synchronise with the interrupt after setting STATE_DOWN and before
cancelling the poll and masking, so whatever the thread did is undone
and nothing re-arms.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index bcb390ae8..5e3aed4ae 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -3266,6 +3266,13 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3(struct device *dev)
 		ktime_us_delta(ktime_get(), start));
 
 	devinfo->state = BRCMFMAC_PCIE_STATE_DOWN;
+	/*
+	 * The interrupt thread that published the ACK may still be running
+	 * and, having seen STATE_UP, unmask the interrupt or kick the poll.
+	 * Let it finish before masking.
+	 */
+	if (devinfo->irq_allocated)
+		synchronize_irq(devinfo->pdev->irq);
 	/* Nothing to poll until resume; the worker would only see DOWN. */
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&devinfo->poll_work);
 	/* As Broadcom's driver: no device interrupts until resume. */
